{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are ThreadSense grounding verifier. You verify independently of the drafting agent; you judge and never repair.\nYour personal goal is: Judge every statement against the full topic context and decide whether the passed premises justify the exact proposed action."},{"role":"user","content":"\nCurrent Task: Judge each statement against the evidence it cites, read within the full context provided: every message of every member thread (with canonical author IDs, roles, thread starters and reactions) and every retrieved source for this topic. Citing a source is not support. A statement is SUPPORTED only if its cited evidence states or directly entails it and nothing in the context contradicts it; PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED if a material part is missing or the context qualifies it; UNSUPPORTED otherwise. A status line marking an excerpt historical, unresolved or a prior record means it cannot support what applies now. By kind: CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT is a report of what members say, not a verified cause; CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT is SUPPORTED if the cited source says it, described with its status and dates; it establishes no current handling, procedure or destination; CLAIM_CAUSE needs verification in the cited evidence; a Verbatim quote must match its source, a Paraphrase must preserve the meaning. Prose names no one: role wording (\"the team lead instructs\", \"a tutor reports\") must match the cited author's role and act (reported, asked, confirmed or instructed), plural wording needs that many distinct cited authors, and listed attributions must hold (AUTHOR wrote the cited message, THREAD_STARTER started its thread, PARTICIPANT posted in it). A retrieved record's authorship is separate from its authority: an approver or recorder (actor_relation RECORD_AUTHORITY) is not its author, and a record whose authorship is not verified names no author. SUMMARY and SEVERITY_RATIONALE must follow from the evidence with no added cause, count or outcome. A SUMMARY sentence (statement_id summary:s1, summary:s2, ...) is judged on its own and shown only if SUPPORTED; its attributions name the people its role wording refers to, and wording that groups several people is SUPPORTED only if what it says they asked or reported is stated in each of their cited messages. A SUMMARY sentence with depends_on is read after the sentences it lists (for words such as \"this\" or \"their\"), but judged only on what it adds. A DETAIL sentence (statement_id detail:d1, detail:d2, ...) is shown when the card is opened and is judged exactly like a SUMMARY sentence: on its own, shown only if SUPPORTED, read after the sentences in its depends_on but judged only on what it adds. NO_ACTION_RATIONALE is the advisor's reason for proposing no further intervention now: SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence shows that reason and the context shows no unresolved handling question, guidance gap, applicable pending decision or operational problem that needs coordination; existing guidance does not by itself establish that no action is needed. ACTION and ALTERNATIVE are recommendations: judge whether their premises are supported, whether the action applies to this topic and whether the rationale follows; a source need not literally prescribe the action. Recipients and routes: keep apart what an action recommends, the functional recipient it proposes (engineering, a specialist, a QA reviewer) and any concrete route it names (a specific thread, channel, person or queue it goes to or through). A proposed functional recipient is justified by supported incident evidence showing a problem that needs that recipient's expertise; evidence of an established intake route is not required, and mentioning the recipient justifies nothing by itself. A concrete route, or a claim that a route is designated, official or mandatory, is a claim of its own and needs a premise whose evidence establishes it; an example-collection or status note asks people where to post examples and does not make that thread an intake route. The recommendation stays advisory (the team lead decides; it need not be shown to be the required or only next step): when no evidence names the concrete route, leave it unspecified (\"report it to engineering\") rather than choosing one. Judge a proposed recipient the same way in ACTION, ALTERNATIVE, INTERVENTION_NEED, ACTION_RATIONALE and REVIEW_NOTE: on whether the incident evidence shows a problem that needs that recipient's expertise, never on whether an intake route is on record; a statement that proposes a recipient and leaves the concrete route unspecified is not PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED, UNSUPPORTED or insufficient for that reason. ACTION and operational ALTERNATIVE statements list their premises: PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT premises are judged here and are provisional, not final; REJECTED ones failed deterministic checks and support nothing; a premise with depends_on stands only if every ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING statement it lists is also SUPPORTED. ACTION_CHOICE is SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence really leaves that choice between the named actions open (not merely an imagined alternative, a review flag or an unknown cause). INTERVENTION_NEED says why intervening now is needed: SUPPORTED only if the context shows that reason (an unresolved handling question, a guidance gap, an applicable pending decision, or an operational problem that needs coordination). Questions already answered in their threads are not unresolved; a general benefit (\"a reminder might help\") is not a need; existing guidance does not by itself rule a need out. Judge in this order: (1) announcement handling; (2) each premise's final status, which is your verdict on it combined with its dependencies; (3) sufficiency. Fill action_sufficiency for the ACTION and one alternative_sufficiency entry (with its statement_id) for each ALTERNATIVE that lists premises: SUFFICIENT only if premises whose final status is SUPPORTED justify the exact text as worded, including its conditions and scope; essential_statement_ids lists the premises it cannot stand without (each must have final status SUPPORTED); INSUFFICIENT if its exact text relies on a rejected, unsupported or dependency-voided premise or goes beyond its premises; a listed premise the text does not rely on is not essential, and its failure alone does not make the action insufficient. ACTION_RATIONALE is judged separately and may also cite context claims; action_sufficiency null if no ACTION statement is sent. SOURCE_AGREEMENT is SUPPORTED only if the named current sources say the same thing on the point in conflict and only the superseded material differs. A request by anyone but a team lead is a CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT: SUPPORTED if that person asked it, and it carries no authority. CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION is a team lead's in-thread instruction: SUPPORTED only if that message gives it and it applies to the threads in scope; it is not project guidance. HISTORICAL_RECURRENCE needs retrieved records of earlier occurrences; REPORTED_RECURRENCE only needs members saying it is happening again. AFFECTED_REPORTER needs that person's own message reporting that they are affected. RESOLUTION is judged against the member's complete thread, including messages the statement did not cite. ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING needs the announcement to give that directive for this topic's project, batch and problem, and it governs only what it directs (a request to post examples governs where examples go, not escalation or an intake route); a routine reminder or schedule directs nothing for the topic. OPEN_QUESTION is SUPPORTED only if the guidance and decisions in the context really leave that specific question unsettled and it is a handling or policy question for the team lead; a not-yet-diagnosed cause, pending diagnostic results or a pending expert assessment is not one. Return exactly one verdict for every statement_id. The team lead reads SUMMARY, DETAIL, ACTION (label, instruction, draft to copy, scope and changes), ACTION_RATIONALE, NO_ACTION_RATIONALE, REVIEW_NOTE and OPEN_QUESTION exactly as written: judge that exact text, including its conditions, uncertainty, scope and who reported, asked, confirmed or instructed; plain wording is expected, but it must not overstate the evidence. A quoted passage must match its source exactly. open_review_flags lists the upstream review obligations still open on these threads; a REVIEW_NOTE may rely on them. Source consistency (always fill source_consistency, even when the draft declares no conflict): compare the governing_sources that address the handling question of this topic with each other, independently of the draft. List sources that state the same rule as AGREE, and sources that state different rules for the same cases as CONFLICT with the point and disagreement_scope (which cases, batch or section differ). assessed_evidence_ids lists the governing sources you compared; relations may be empty when they address different points. Only governing sources count: historical, superseded, expired or withdrawn material, prior records and member messages are not current sources, an announcement governs only if it directs handling for this topic, and members disagreeing with each other is not a source conflict. For each entry in declared_conflicts give one declared_conflict_checks entry: CONFIRMED (the cited sources state different rules on that point), SOURCES_AGREE (they say the same thing; only wording or detail differs) or UNDETERMINED.\n\nInput JSON:\n{\"topic\": {\"project_id\": \"audio_multimodal\", \"batch_id\": \"audio_batch_06\", \"candidate_group_id\": \"cluster_3a9de1cf4cf6b8d4\", \"topic_id\": \"cluster_3a9de1cf4cf6b8d4/topic_1\", \"topic_label\": \"LT player fails to load audio\", \"projection_gap\": null, \"as_of\": \"2026-10-02T12:00:00Z\", \"member_ids\": [\"member_8ce5853bbd6b1a416c28b76f\", \"member_e0275e7d53c557361ca40bd1\", \"member_0e456786d757d2f8f71957dd\", \"member_a1e89672d04665844a7d82e6\", \"member_943da52557c55ff31ee76f89\"]}, \"statements\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor reports that the player never loads in one thread and remains on the spinner after opening a task in another; the QA tutor asks about QN or correct handling and recalls a possible workaround from the previous queue.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790882197.000111\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790916069.000107\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U019\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790882197.000111\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U019\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790916069.000107\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports that audio will not play in LT on AUDIO-6012, asks whether this is QN or a player issue, and recalls a possible workaround from the previous queue.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790896012.001900\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U018\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790896012.001900\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor reports a blank player on three items, references AUDIO-9653, and asks whether continuing tasking is safe.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790919653.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U014\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790919653.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports in the blank-player thread that the waveform loads but pressing Play never starts sound, and asks whether the waveform loads while the playhead stays at zero.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790919698.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U015\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790919698.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports that the player never loads, asks whether to QN, and recalls a possible workaround from the previous queue.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790920171.000109\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U020\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790920171.000109\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"Current project instructions require reporting unavailable playback, including a visible waveform without playback, as a tool incident with the task ID; capturing browser/error state and whether another clip plays; and not assigning model-quality failure or content QN solely because playback is unavailable. Old workarounds must be checked against current symptoms, and handling guidance does not establish repair or evaluability.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3:1c6df70e\", \"k:audio-multimodal-faq@1.1:c724358c\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c7\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION\", \"text\": \"In the first never-loading-player thread, the team lead requires task IDs and a reproduction attempt before deciding whether the old workaround applies, and says to retain both task references if another clip plays.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790882343.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790882343.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c8\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION\", \"text\": \"In the AUDIO-6012 thread, the team lead requires task IDs and a reproduction attempt before deciding whether the old workaround applies, and asks whether the waveform loads but the playhead stays at zero.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790896106.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790896106.000226\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c9\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION\", \"text\": \"In the persistent-spinner thread, the team lead requires task IDs and a reproduction attempt before deciding whether the old workaround applies, and cautions that the spinner does not establish the underlying audio's contents.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790916217.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790916217.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c10\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION\", \"text\": \"In the blank-player thread and the later never-loading-player thread, the team lead says the affected task cannot be evaluated while playback fails, instructs reporting the playback incident with its task ID, and prohibits treating it as a model-quality failure.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790919745.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790920220.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790919745.000226\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790920220.000113\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c11\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"An engineer asks for the LT error state and time on AUDIO-2197 in the first never-loading-player thread and on AUDIO-6069 in the persistent-spinner thread; the engineer says the wider cause is not confirmed.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790882287.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790916165.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U016\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790882287.000226\", \"role\": \"ENGINEER\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U016\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790916165.000226\", \"role\": \"ENGINEER\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c12\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INFERENCE\", \"text\": \"The provided threads contain no posted playback recovery confirmation, and the first three threads contain no supplied reproduction results or responses completing the requested diagnostics.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790882197.000111\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790882245.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790882287.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790882343.000339\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790896012.001900\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790896062.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790896106.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790916069.000107\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790916120.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790916165.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790916217.000339\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790919653.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790919698.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790919745.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790920171.000109\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790920220.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c13\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The current batch handling reminder directs reporting the task ID, browser/error state, and whether another clip plays when LT playback never starts, including when a waveform is visible; it treats this as a tool incident, not grounds alone for model-quality failure or content QN, and does not confirm repair.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:slack:C_AUDIO_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790892000.000901:1c524924\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"k:slack:C_AUDIO_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790892000.000901:1c524924\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c14\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT\", \"text\": \"The October 1 batch status announcement states that a previously attempted fix did not resolve the player failure and asks for examples in its thread while scope is checked; that request establishes an example-collection destination, not an engineering intake route.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:slack:C_AUDIO_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790890099.000112:64d38d33\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"k:slack:C_AUDIO_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790890099.000112:64d38d33\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c15\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_HISTORY\", \"text\": \"The earlier batch announcement authorized at most one reload as a diagnostic trial for a player stuck at 00:00 through August 28, required retaining diagnostic details and reporting continued playback failure, and explicitly did not establish a repair. Its authorization has expired, and its recorded outcome was not observed.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:audio-playback-trial-post@1.0:d674dbe6\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"k:audio-playback-trial-post@1.0:d674dbe6\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s1\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"Two QA tutors and three tutors report unavailable playback in LT, including a player that never loads, a persistent spinner, a blank player, and a waveform without sound.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790882197.000111\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790916069.000107\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790896012.001900\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790919653.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790919698.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790920171.000109\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U019\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790882197.000111\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U019\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790916069.000107\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U018\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790896012.001900\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U014\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790919653.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U015\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790919698.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U020\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790920171.000109\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s2\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"Current guidance treats unavailable playback as a tool incident, not grounds alone for content QN; the reported failures have no posted recovery confirmation.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3:1c6df70e\", \"k:audio-multimodal-faq@1.1:c724358c\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790882197.000111\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790882245.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790882287.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790882343.000339\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790896012.001900\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790896062.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790896106.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790916069.000107\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790916120.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790916165.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790916217.000339\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790919653.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790919698.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790919745.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790920171.000109\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790920220.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d1\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor reports a player that never loads in one thread and stays on the spinner in a second thread.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790882197.000111\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790916069.000107\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U019\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790882197.000111\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U019\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790916069.000107\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d2\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports no playback on AUDIO-6012, while a QA tutor reports a blank player on three items and references AUDIO-9653.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790896012.001900\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790919653.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U018\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790896012.001900\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U014\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790919653.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d3\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports that the waveform loads but pressing Play produces no sound; a different tutor reports that the player never loads.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790919698.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790920171.000109\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U015\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790919698.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U020\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790920171.000109\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d4\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The team lead requested diagnostic inputs in the first three threads before deciding whether the old workaround applies; those inputs have not been posted in those threads.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790882343.000339\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790896106.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790916217.000339\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790882197.000111\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790882245.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790882287.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790896012.001900\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790896062.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790916069.000107\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790916120.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790916165.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790919653.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790919698.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790919745.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790920171.000109\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790920220.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790882343.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790896106.000226\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790916217.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d5\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The team lead answered the affected-task handling questions in the blank-player thread and the later never-loading-player thread, instructing the thread starters to report playback incidents rather than model-quality failures.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790919745.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790920220.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790919745.000226\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790920220.000113\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d6\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"An earlier batch announcement authorized a time-limited one-reload diagnostic trial, not a confirmed repair; its recorded outcome was not observed, and its authorization expired on August 28.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:audio-playback-trial-post@1.0:d674dbe6\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"k:audio-playback-trial-post@1.0:d674dbe6\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action\", \"kind\": \"ACTION\", \"text\": \"Report a technical issue to engineering. Instruction: Report the playback failures together to engineering, keeping each symptom and task reference distinct and identifying the diagnostic inputs still outstanding. Draft to copy: Engineering, please investigate these LT playback reports from two QA tutors and three tutors:\\n- A QA tutor reports never-loading playback and, in a second thread, a persistent spinner; the engineer's requests reference AUDIO-2197 and AUDIO-6069.\\n- A tutor reports no playback on AUDIO-6012.\\n- A QA tutor reports a blank player on three items, referencing AUDIO-9653.\\n- A tutor in that thread reports a visible waveform but no sound after pressing Play.\\n- A tutor in the later thread reports that the player never loads.\\n\\nPlease check these failures as tool incidents. Current guidance calls for task IDs, browser/error state, and whether another clip plays. The engineer requested error state and time specifically for AUDIO-2197 and AUDIO-6069. In the first three threads, I still need task IDs and a reproduction attempt before assessing the old workaround. For AUDIO-6012, also note whether the waveform loads while the playhead stays at zero; in the AUDIO-2197 thread, retain both task references if another clip plays. Scope: Investigate the reported playback failures without assuming a shared cause, a confirmed repair, or that the expired reload trial applies now.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790882197.000111\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790916069.000107\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790896012.001900\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790919653.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790919698.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790920171.000109\", \"k:audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3:1c6df70e\", \"k:audio-multimodal-faq@1.1:c724358c\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790882343.000339\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790896106.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790916217.000339\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790882287.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790916165.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790882245.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790896062.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790916120.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790919745.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790920220.000113\", \"k:audio-playback-trial-post@1.0:d674dbe6\"], \"premises\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}